  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `billing/payments.py`, in `collect()`. All 24 existing tests pass. I didn't add your reproduction test to the suite, so I haven't run it.\n\n**Root cause:** when a retry payment succeeded, `collect()` marked the invoice paid but never moved the subscription back to `active`. The recovery function `recover()` in `dunning.py` was never called anywhere. A stray `pass` sat where the call belonged, so the subscription stayed `past_due`.\n\n**Fix:** I replaced that `pass` with `recover(ctx, invoice)` and imported `recover` from `dunning`.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repo root: `{\"file\": \"payments.py\", \"function\": \"collect\"}`.",
